From 49d401b344a25e1064d8310643f753dd901cf067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] widescreen auto-UI: squash slanted front overlays as HUD,
 keep edge vertices

Under auto_ui_provenance a screen-space triangle or slanted quad drawn in
front of every world primitive is now a HUD candidate in its own right,
not only a part lying inside an admitted widget. A vertex on or beyond a
display edge keeps its X, so an overlay covering the 4:3 screen out to its
edges still reaches the edges of the wide image after the inner part is
squashed.

Fixes Action Man: Mission Xtreme's bow scope at 16:9: the mask is a radial
mesh of slanted quads with a few axis-aligned ones among them, and only
those were squashed, which tore holes in the mask, left the zoom meter
squashed inside a stretched panel and split the first-person bow's wings.
New test: ws_auto_ui_overlay_mesh_exec_test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
